feat(compose): upload progress overlay on /compose

Per Dan's ask: "ADD THE CLOCK OR SOME KIND OF ANYTHING THAT TELLS THE
USER THAT IT'S WORKING AND UPLOADING. IT EXISTED ONCE, THEN IT WAS GONE."

The old inline composer showed a progress banner during upload; the new
/compose page route silently held inFlight without any visual feedback
beyond a greyed-out "Posting..." button. 5-15s preflight + a 16 MB-chunk
TUS upload that can take 30s+ on cellular with no indicator = user thinks
the app froze and starts mashing buttons.

Three layers:

1. composeStore.js -- three new fields + setters:
     uploadPct (0-100), uploadLabel, uploadStage
     ('preflight' | 'uploading' | 'creating' | 'finishing')

2. compose.js handlePostNow -- subscribes to bgUpload's onProgress and
   writes overall percent across multi-file uploads. Stage transitions:
   preflight -> uploading -> creating -> finishing. Image-only path seeds
   0 percent + 'Uploading photo' so the overlay shows immediately.

3. EditPostScreen.jsx -- fullscreen z-index 99999 overlay when inFlight:
     - 48px Facebook-blue spinner (spPrepSpin keyframe)
     - Stage-aware title (Preparing / Uploading your video / Almost done
       / Creating your post)
     - Determinate bar during upload, indeterminate sweep during
       creating/finishing
     - Big tabular-nums percent (22px FB blue) during upload/preflight
     - uploadLabel below with pulse animation
     - Reassurance: Keep this screen open. We'll let you know when
       it's posted.
   Backdrop rgba(15,16,20,0.78) + 6px blur, matching FB's overlay
   weight.

esbuild parsed the new file cleanly. WebAudio chirp + broadcastSync
unchanged.
